⍝ Quad_ES_issuer.tc
⍝ ----------------------------------

⍝@ test3.

      ⍝ lrm p.282: when ⎕ES is executed from within a defined function,
      ⍝ the event is generated as though the function (the "issuer")
      ⍝ were primitive. Suspension occurs at the calling point, so the
      ⍝ error message shows the issuer's CALLING statement. A ⎕ES that
      ⍝ is executed via ⍎ (or in A of ⎕EA) inside a function counts as
      ⍝ executed within that function (confirmed with IBM APL2).
      ⍝
      ⍝ The cases are captured with 3⊃⎕EC so that they can also be run
      ⍝ (and compared) with IBM APL2 via MEGA11 (testcases_apl2), which
      ⍝ records statement values but not error displays or )SI.
      ⍝
      ⍝ Compared with IBM APL2 via MEGA11 (2026-10-02): rows 1-3 of ⎕EM
      ⍝ agree for every case below (including the single caret, e.g.
      ⍝ under EXPO 0), except for two general display differences that
      ⍝ are unrelated to ⎕ES: IBM APL2 shows the entire ◊-line T3[1]
      ⍝ 'x'◊U◊'y' (GNU APL: only the failed statement U), and its ⎕EM
      ⍝ has two more rows for the outer statement (e.g. W ^) when the
      ⍝ issuer was called from another defined function.

      )ERASE TEST W EXPO V U T3 T4 W4

∇TEST
 ⍎'⎕ES ''HELLO'''
∇

∇W
 TEST
∇

∇Z←EXPO A
 ⎕ES(0=A)/'ZERO INVALID'
 Z←⋆A
∇

∇V
 EXPO 0
∇

∇U
 ⎕ES 5 4
∇

∇T3
 'x' ◊ U ◊ 'y'
∇

∇T4
 '⎕ES ''HELLO''' ⎕EA '3÷0'
∇

∇W4
 T4
∇

      ⍝ ⎕ES via ⍎ in TEST, TEST called from immediate execution
      ⍝
      3⊃⎕EC 'TEST'
HELLO
      TEST
      ^

      ⍝ ... TEST called from W
      ⍝
      3⊃⎕EC 'W'
HELLO
W[1]  TEST
      ^

      ⍝ ⎕ES directly in EXPO, EXPO called from immediate execution
      ⍝
      3⊃⎕EC 'EXPO 0'
ZERO INVALID
      EXPO 0
      ^

      ⍝ ... EXPO called from V
      ⍝
      3⊃⎕EC 'V'
ZERO INVALID
V[1]  EXPO 0
      ^

      ⍝ ⎕ES directly in U, U called from T3 (after 'x', before 'y')
      ⍝
      3⊃⎕EC 'T3'
x
DOMAIN ERROR
T3[1]  U
       ^

      ⍝ ⎕ES in A of ⎕EA in T4, T4 called from immediate execution
      ⍝
      3⊃⎕EC 'T4'
HELLO
      T4
      ^

      ⍝ ... T4 called from W4
      ⍝
      3⊃⎕EC 'W4'
HELLO
W4[1]  T4
       ^

      )ERASE TEST W EXPO V U T3 T4 W4

      ⍝ ==================================

